  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Classification contract",
      "items": [
        "LLM #1 returns 11 fields. HSBC and UNCERTAIN have six null Supplier fields; SUPPLIER uses documented facts, Unknown for missing core facts.",
        "UNCERTAIN is successful abstention. Attribution evidence strength is 0–4, not probability: UNCERTAIN 0–2; HSBC / SUPPLIER 1–4.",
        "Python validates exact evidence names and score consistency. INCIDENT_ID stays local. Save source columns and one comma-separated evidence_column."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "The second LLM call is conditional",
      "items": [
        "Only successful SUPPLIER rows enter name matching. Normalize names for matching only; inspect THIRD_PARTY_NAME before THIRD_PARTY_NORMALISED_NAME.",
        "Keep the first 70 matches by default, in ENG_ALL order. This is a candidate cap, not relevance ranking. Send complete shortlisted rows with incident context.",
        "A nonempty shortlist permits LLM #2. Select one supplied ID or null; Python validates the decision and copies real engagement fields. No invented engagement."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Every processed row is retained",
      "items": [
        "HSBC bypasses search and call #2: NOT_APPLICABLE. UNCERTAIN and failed classification: SKIPPED. These rows still reach INC_LINKED.csv.",
        "No candidates or an undecided model selection: UNDECIDED. Valid selection: MATCHED. Request or validation error: FAILED; save where possible, then stop.",
        "Link evidence strength is separately 0–4: selected ID 1–4; null 0–2. No call means no score. Earlier saved rows and source CSVs remain intact."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Two views, one human decision store",
      "items": [
        "Incident first shows all saved incidents, classification counts and Supplier linking totals. Engagement first opens engagements, then their incidents.",
        "Engagement first includes zero-incident ENG_ALL entries and saved proposal IDs missing from the catalog. If catalog loading fails, show saved proposals with a scope warning.",
        "Both views share details, Yes/No controls and HUMAN_REVIEW.csv. Global Confirmed / Pending / Rejected / Invalidated counts remain separate from original model counts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Review rules preserve model proposals",
      "items": [
        "Classification No requires a reason and invalidates an existing proposal. Confirming it again resets the invalidated link to Pending.",
        "Link review requires confirmed SUPPLIER classification and an existing matched proposal. Link No requires a reason and leaves classification confirmed.",
        "Only both confirmations fill hitl_linked_engagement_id. HSBC / UNCERTAIN have no link review. Original model labels, scores and ENG_ fields are preserved; no FINAL.csv."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Shared request budgets",
      "items": [
        ".env defaults: LLM_MAX_INPUT_TOKENS=32000 and LLM_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=2000. Both are positive integers and apply to both calls.",
        "Input is estimated locally over prompt, fields, candidate rows and response schema. Over budget: no request and no truncation. It is not exact provider usage.",
        "Output uses max_completion_tokens, including reasoning where applicable. Incomplete JSON is rejected. The 70-candidate cap is independent of token limits."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Source and scope",
      "items": [
        "Based on the current local docs/short_desription.md, frozen alongside this diagram. Source references point to that isolated documentation snapshot, not a published application commit.",
        "The flow starts at CLEAN.csv. Upstream read / rename / clean is outside this view. Classification, linking and review are separate manually run stages.",
        "This is a documented logical flow, not a live execution or measured result. Dashboards 8766 and 8767 are read-only; review makes no LLM call. No sample counts are presented as actual results."
      ]
    }
  ]
